# Keeps the Docker build context for design/packages/cli/Dockerfile small. The
# Dockerfile COPYs only the specific paths it needs (design/package.json,
# design/packages, design/tools, vendor/BlueMap/common/webapp/dist); everything
# below would otherwise still be walked and hashed into the build context,
# which is real, measured cost — a first build here spent about 50 seconds
# just transferring context before this file existed, dominated by node_modules
# and the vendored Java toolchain state, none of which any Dockerfile stage
# actually reads.
**/node_modules/
design/packages/*/dist/
design/tools/*/dist/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.git/
# The webapp is built inside the image from its own source, so its prebuilt dist/
# is deliberately NOT un-excluded here any more: shipping a stale locally-built
# bundle into the context would let a warm machine build a different image from the
# one a clean checkout builds, which is exactly the difference this file's own
# reproducibility depends on. The build stage produces dist/ itself.
vendor/BlueMap/common/webapp/dist/

# The Java oracle harness's own downloaded toolchain and Gradle state
# (gigabyte-scale; see the matching entries in .gitignore).
tools/oracle/.gradle/
tools/oracle/jdk/
tools/oracle/out/
vendor/BlueMap/**/build/
vendor/BlueMap/.gradle/
vendor/BlueMap/**/node_modules/

# Never bundle a BlueMap render's own output or Mojang download into an image.
/web/
/data/
test-world/
*.mca
